  "explanation": "Substituting into $f(a) = 9(4)^a = 576$ and dividing by $9$ yields $(4)^a = 64 = 4^3$, so $a = 3$. Similarly, from $f(b) = 9(4)^b = 2304$, dividing by $9$ gives $(4)^b = 256 = 4^4$, so $b = 4$. Therefore, $b - a = 4 - 3 = 1$.\n\nWhy B is incorrect:\n\nThis may result from an arithmetic error when solving for $a$, such as incorrectly determining that $4^2 = 64$, which would give $a = 2$ and thus $b - a = 4 - 2 = 2$.",
